  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MTAANI YOUTH SPORTS DEVELOPMENT</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project seeks to combat drug abuse and crime among male and female  youth in Nairobi&apos;s selected informal settlements through innovative sports-based interventions that aim to strengthen governance and democracy. Located in Kaloleni, Huruma, and Mathare slums, this project targets 300 youth 14-25yrs  facing  multiple vulnerabilities  e.g unemployment, limited educational opportunities, exposure to drug abuse and criminal activities. The project will establish six community-led sports clubs as platforms for civic education, leadership development, and democratic engagement, creating sustainable pathways for youth empowerment.</narrative>
  </description>
